SUMMARY:FYI: What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**For Oct 22 thru Oct 28**\n\nUpcoming **mu
 sic events** may be found here:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/\
 n(Updates on Thurs morning)\n\n**Assorted entertainment\, festival & marke
 t events may be found here:**\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/calendar-
 of-events\n\n**Library programs** may be found here:\nhttps://hendersonpl.
 libcal.com/\n\n**Wednesday\, October 14**\nJason DeCristofaro's Jazz Night
 \n6-8pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n\
 n**Oct 22**\nCroquet & Bocce ball at Jackson Pk\nOct & Nov schedule\nhttps
 ://www.hendersoncountync.gov/recreation\n**Fri\; Oct 23**\n**Hospice Wareh
 ouse sale\; Oct 23 & 24. (**(3rd Fri/Sat of mnth)\nYou'll find a wide vari
 ety of value furniture items at the warehouse. Shop with us each month whe
 n we host our 2-day warehouse sales and support the care services of Four 
 Seasons.\n9:00 AM - 2:00 PM\; 561 S Allen Rd\, Flat Rock\nhttps://www.face
 book.com/HospiceHomeStore\n**October 23** @ 6:00 pm - 9:00 pm\; Free\n3 Sh
 ades of Gray: Live at Trailside Brewing Co.\nBandmates Bob Zullo (Guitar &
  Vocal)\, Dex Stutzman (Guitar\, Keys\, Harp & Vocal) & James Leyva (Guita
 r & Vocal) focusing on vocal harmonies of the 70’s and beyond. Playing 
 “pop” tunes from the Beatles & CSNY to Jason Isbell……..and a few o
 riginals thrown in.\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/3-shades-of-g
 ray-live-at-trailside-brewing-co\nhttps://www.facebook.com/events/14039702
 51244246\n**October 24** @ 12:00 pm - 3:00 pm\; Free\nFall Mountain Music 
 Gathering & Free Community Meal in **Etowah.**\nhttps://visithendersonvill
 enc.org/event/meet-me-in-etowah-fall-mountain-music-gathering-free-communi
 ty-meal\n**October 24\;** Free\nGHOULFEST IS COMING!\nGet ready for a spoo
 ky Sunday at Ecusta Market Cafe & Trailside Brewing Co. on October 24th\, 
 11AM–5PM!\n35+ local vendors\nLive music with Kate Bryant 12–2PM + Jos
 h Dunkin 3–5PM\nSpooky scavenger hunt\; Costume contest\; Face painting\
 nCold drinks + good food\nAnd plenty of Halloween fun!\n441 S Whitted St\,
  Hendersonville\, NC\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/halloween-go
 ulfest-at-trailside-brewing\n**October 24** @ 6:00 pm - 9:00 pm\; Free\nPa
 rker’s Back Vintage Jazz at Trailside Brewing\nJoin us for an evening of
  timeless tunes and toe-tapping rhythms with Parker’s Back\, a string tr
 io bringing vintage vocal jazz\, swing\, and Gypsy Jazz classics to life 
 — from the 1920s onward.\nFeaturing:\nRobbie Grice – guitar & vocals\;
  Alex Travers – violin\; James Dawkins – upright bass\nWhether you’r
 e a fan of Django-style swing\, smooth jazz standards\, or just looking fo
 r a fun night out\, you’ll love the energy and charm of this WNC-based t
 rio.\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/parkers-back-vintage-jazz-at
 -trailside-brewing\n**Saturday\, October 24**\nThe Showboat Band\n6-9pm\, 
 Bold Rock Hard Cidery\, 72 School House Rd\, Mills River\n**Saturday\, Oct
 ober 24**\nMountain Shag Club Halloween Party (With DJ Tommy Samole)\n6-10
 pm\, Hendersonville Elks Lodge\, 546 North Justice St\, Hendersonville NC 
 28739\nCostume Contest and bring a snack to share. FREE for members and $1
 0 for Guests.\n**Saturday\, October 24**\nFine Line\n6-10pm\, J&M Farms\, 
 3016 Chimney Rock Road\, Hendersonville\n**Sunday\, October 25**\nHenderso
 nville Ballroom Dance Club Tea Dance - Dress: Latin look – Fringe or Ruf
 fles\n3-5:30pm\, Upstairs at Hedrick Rhodes Veterans Center\, 900 North Ma
 in St\, Hendersonville NC 28792\n3pm - Cha Cha Dance Lesson with Carrie Fe
 rnandez.\nAmple parking at the front entry of the building\, take the elev
 ator or stairs to the upper level. Parking is\nlimited at the rear entranc
 e\, both front and back doors will be unlocked. 3-5:30pm - Open Ballroom D
 ance to\nthe music of DJ Gary Bills. Our dances are open to the public and
  everyone is invited. Enjoy Ballroom\nDancing to the music of DJ Gary Bill
 s who plays a variety of dance tunes including Swing (East & West\nCoast)\
 , Waltz\, Tango\, Rumba\, Cha-Cha and Foxtrot. There is also a dance mixer
  Cost: $5 per person at\ndoor.\n**Sunday\, October 25**\nSundayFunday Pegg
 y Ratusz @ SAB\; 4-6PM\nSouthern Appalachian Brewery\; 822 Locust St. Hend
 ersonville\n**Wednesday\, October 28**\nJason DeCristofaro's Jazz Night (E
 ach Wednesday)\n6-8pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hen
 dersonville\n**Wednesday\, October 28**\nWeekly Westie Wednesdays (Ages 21
  & Up) (Each Wednesday)\n7-10pm\, Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\,
  Suite 101\, Hendersonville NC 28792\n7-8pm - Continuation Lesson & 7:30-8
 pm - Beginner Lesson. 8-10pm - Social Dance.\nLessons rotate weekly with o
 ur incredible instructor lineup: Ryan Pflumm\, Jason Barnes\, Jenna Shimek
 \,\nMissy Lindsey\, Rachel Harris\, Tom and Janet Leazenby\, and Tola Sun 
 - all bringing fresh energy and\nperspectives each week! Enjoy a rotation 
 of community DJs keeping the vibes high and the floor full all night\nlong
 . No outside drinks (including water bottles) - water station available. O
 utside food welcome. Dress is\ncasual and No partner needed! Dedicated par
 king next to the venue & street parking. Please help us\nsupport our amazi
 ng host venue by grabbing a drink or snack at the bar - it helps keep danc
 e nights thriving!\nPricing: $10 lesson & social\, $5 social only\n**Thu\;
  October 29\; 6 PM**\nEllen\, Howie & Woody\nSouthern Appalachian Brewery\
 ; 822 Locust St. Hendersonville\n**Friday\, October 30**\nBlake Ellege\n8-
 11pm\, Oklawaha Brewery\, 147 First Ave East\, Hendersonville\n**October 3
 1 @ 3:00 pm - 4:30 pm**\nReader’s Theatre – **War of the Worlds\, The 
 1938 Radio Script**\n**Tickets:** https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/re
 aders-theatre-war-of-the-worlds\nBroadcast from New York’s Mercury Theat
 re in 1938\, this infamous radio play\, based on the novel by H. G. Wells\
 , had many terrified listeners convinced that an actual alien invasion of 
 Earth was taking place. Adapted by Howard E. Koch\, co-writer of Casablanc
 a\, and directed and narrated by Orson Welles\, this original script detai
 ling the frightening tale of an extraterrestrial takeover is now available
  to bring to life onstage to thrill and chill audiences.\nhttps://visithen
 dersonvillenc.org/event/readers-theatre-war-of-the-worlds-the-1938-radio-s
 cript/2026-10-31\nhttps://hendersonvilletheatre.org/readers-theatre-war-of
 -the-worlds-the-1938-radio-script/\n**Saturday\, October 31**\nTreat Stree
 t\; 2:00 pm - 5:00 pm\; Free\nJoin for Kids Fun Zone – Sponsored by Bilt
 more Church\, Trick-Or-Treating\, DJ Dance Party\, Costume contest\, Games
  and more.\n**Saturday\, October 31**\nSaints & Sinners - Halloween Costum
 e Party\n6-10pm\, Sissy’s/J&M Farms\, 3016 Chimney Rock Road\, Henderson
 ville\n**Saturday\, October 31**\nFlashback Band Halloween Extravaganza\n6
 :30-9:30pm\, Mills River Brewery\, 336 Banner Farm Rd\, Mills River\n**Oct
 ober 31** @ 6:00 pm - 9:00 pm\; Free\nHalloween Party at Trailside Brewing
  Co.\na spooktacular night of music\, costumes\, and Halloween fun at Trai
 lside Brewing with Steve Weams and The Ghouls!\nLive Music: Steve Weams Ba
 nd and the Ghouls\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/halloween-party
 -at-trailside-brewing-co\n\nThese are NOT hosted events and are posted for
  informational purposes only. Please make personal arrangements to meetup 
 with friends and family.\nIf you wish to attend and host one of these even
 ts\, I will post the event as an individual happening. Hosting only requir
 es being focal point for others and making introductions. Simple!!
