SUMMARY:DuPont/Cedar Rock Mtn\; a Saunter
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nI am going to Cedar Rock Mtn in DuPont Fore
 st\; Up to 12 ppl are welcome to join.\nCedar Rock Mountain in DuPont Stat
 e Forest provides wonderful views and dramatic scenery - Cedar Rock Mounta
 in contains some of the most exposed granite anywhere in the region. Hundr
 eds of acres alternate between bare and moss/lichen covered rock. The area
  has become quite popular with mountain bikers and hikers.\nWe will walk t
 he Big Rock/ Cedar Rock/Little River/Corn Mill Shoals Tr(s).\nRemember - h
 ikes led by ‘the Curmudgeon’ tend to have pleasant surprises.\n**I wil
 l be carrying the ‘Ent-Ward’ that gives us permission to pass thru the
  forest.**\nDifficulty: eroded water outwash on uphill trail. Some rocks &
  roots.\nWe are the Sloth Hike Team of WNC: “We will get there when we g
 et there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ hike groups don’t !!\n**
 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQ8H4EK2vt4**\nDetails:\n(Social ‘hour
 ’ at 9:45 AM. Bus leaves at 9:55a)\nLength: 3.5 mi loop\; accum ascent: 
 550 ft\; Pace: 1.5 mph\n**Drive time: ½ hr/20 mi 1-way\;**\n**Return Not 
 earlier than: 2:30 pm (+4hrs)**\nCarpool contributions appreciated. $3.00 
 suggested\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event is NOT for those
  who are uncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs. Dogs (and Maste
 rs) required to be ‘on-leash' in DuPont. Small (lap)dogs may carpool. La
 rge dogs will drive themselves.\n**Trailhead:** Corn Mills Shoals Access\;
  35.172752\, -82.638705\nGoogle Map =“ Dupont State Recreational Forest\
 , Corn Mill Shoals Access Parking”\nWeather Check: Cedar Rock\, NC\nWAIT
 LISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 2.5 driv
 er(s) (=10ppl)\nIncessant prattlers will be assumed to be having an affair
 .\nWe suggest slightly open windows while carpooling. Only you know your o
 wn health status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your health
  or the health of others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid br
 inging your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nAll
  hikes are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and a
 dequate equipment.\nWaiver: The organizer of this event is a volunteer and
  not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organi
 ze this event. There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity. E
 ach participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to release f
 rom liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliate
 s\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss whi
 ch might occur while participating in this activity or while traveling in 
 any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further agrees to abide b
 y the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow instructions of 
 the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated from the group.*
 * The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collected on this tri
 p for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: Curmudgeo
 nHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)\n**
 Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
